# External drive backups (Windows)

## When to back up

If **`D:\`** exists, is writable, and looks like the user’s external disk (volume label **External** when queryable), treat backups as expected—not optional—for **meaningful work** (multi-file edits, refactors, dependency or native project changes, or anything the user could not trivially redo). After such work, **run an incremental backup** without being asked, unless the user declined backups for this session.

If **`D:\`** is missing or not writable, say the external drive does not appear connected and **do not** fail the task; skip backup.

